      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "yes, please.\n\ni am aware that increasing the cap may break some Udon mechanics, especially in game worlds, but simply put: i don't care. a proper warning for that is needed for sure, but that's not a blocker.\n\nlarger caps are needed to visit many worlds with larger groups (it's crazy how many worlds are just inaccessible with 30+ people on a meetup).\n\non the other hand, smaller caps are needed for more introvertic/socially-anxious people, who don't mind people freely coming over, even friends of friends, but just don't want the instance to turn into a convention.\n\nworld creators often misuse the capacity, setting it based on their own misconceptions, like their own hardware and poorly optimized avatars.\n\nplease let the self-conscious users take the risk of potentially breaking something for themselves.\n\nthe cap set by the world creator should be present in public instances, and should be the default for all others, but it definitely should be changeable at instance creation.\n\nit would also alleviate issues with, for example \"Community Meetups\", where people sometimes forget to set the cap to 80 before testing it during the event - they would be able to just set it live for that one instance.\n\nof course the maximum capacity of 80, or however many VRChat changes it to with time, would still remain as a hard limit for people without extra permissions.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
